WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.456 --> 00:00:04.037
-The Taliban have regained
control in Afghanistan,

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:06.439
amid a chaotic U.S. evacuation,
bringing a tragic end

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:09.208
to a 20-year bipartisan
foreign-policy disaster

00:00:09.208 --> 00:00:11.044
that American officials
of both parties

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:12.679
bear responsibility for

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:14.547
and which they have
repeatedly lied about.

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:16.582
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:16.582 --> 00:00:20.320
[ Theme music plays ]

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:23.456
The crushing reality of the
so-called global war on terror

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:25.257
is that some of the
highest-ranking officials

00:00:25.257 --> 00:00:28.394
involved in it now admit
that it was a colossal failure,

00:00:28.394 --> 00:00:30.496
and that's a reality
we should all grapple with.

00:00:30.496 --> 00:00:32.865
Presidents, politicians, and
foreign-policy elites

00:00:32.865 --> 00:00:35.501
of both parties
deserve blame for this calamity.

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:37.036
In his new book,
"Reign of Terror,"

00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:38.838
author Spencer Ackerman writes,

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:40.840
"In 2020, I asked
Stanley McChrystal,

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.975
the former Joint Special
Operations Command

00:00:42.975 --> 00:00:44.410
and Afghanistan War Commander,

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:46.145
if the War on Terror
had been worth it.

00:00:46.145 --> 00:00:48.415
'It would be impossible to argue
that it was,' he answered.

00:00:48.415 --> 00:00:52.151
'The outcome just hasn't been
positive enough to argue that.'"

00:00:52.151 --> 00:00:54.820
That's not an anti-war activist
saying that.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:57.090
That's a former commander
of the war in Afghanistan

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:00.292
saying the 20-year War on Terror
was a failure.

00:01:00.292 --> 00:01:02.528
It's like if Kevin Feige said,
"Honestly, I have no idea

00:01:02.528 --> 00:01:04.197
what's going on in the
Marvel cinematic universe.

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:05.398
None of it makes sense to me.

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:06.732
I mean, they
all have superpowers,

00:01:06.732 --> 00:01:07.934
but every fight
comes down to karate?

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:09.568
What the hell, right?"
Of course, in reality,

00:01:09.568 --> 00:01:11.471
the only thing
Feige has to apologize for

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:14.106
is not putting Vince Vaughn
in Loki.

00:01:14.106 --> 00:01:16.943
You missed a huge opportunity
to create some buzz

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:19.144
and reunite the greatest comic
duo since Laurel and Hardy.

00:01:19.144 --> 00:01:20.313
"Buddy, buddy, buddy.

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:21.847
And I say that because
there are three of you."

00:01:21.847 --> 00:01:26.052
I'm sorry to reference 2005's
"Wedding Crashers."

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:27.419
That movie is so old,
it came out

00:01:27.419 --> 00:01:30.356
four years after the start
of the war in Afghanistan.

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:32.458
A comment like that
from McChrystal,

00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:34.560
the idea that the so-called
War on Terror

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.229
has been a 20-year failure
should provoke

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:38.264
some serious introspection
and soul-searching

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:40.166
on the part of
Washington elites.

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:42.368
And yet somehow
I can't exactly imagine

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:44.270
the people responsible
for this calamity

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:47.006
looking inward and holding
themselves accountable for it.

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:49.508
George W. Bush is too busy
in his art studio,

00:01:49.508 --> 00:01:52.111
trying to, I don't know,
get a dog's eyebrow right.

00:01:52.111 --> 00:01:54.447
So strange that
sandwiched between

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:56.116
James Patterson's co-author

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:58.184
and New England's
newest party promoter,

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:01.487
we have a former President
who's just okay at painting.

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:05.624
Also, were the dogs
supposed to look like him?

00:02:05.624 --> 00:02:08.094
I'm not crazy, right?

00:02:08.094 --> 00:02:11.064
Doesn't it kind of look like
the dogs have Bush's face?

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:13.599
And that expression of his
that says,

00:02:13.599 --> 00:02:15.935
"I don't know the answer
to your question"?

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:17.136
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.136 --> 00:02:19.305
And, yet, as tragedy unfolds
in Afghanistan,

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:20.940
the political world is,
of course,

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.474
engaged in finger-pointing

00:02:22.474 --> 00:02:25.445
for what has been a generational
bipartisan failure

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:27.546
that presidents and politicians
of both parties

00:02:27.546 --> 00:02:28.614
bear responsibility for.

00:02:28.614 --> 00:02:30.617
For example, over the weekend

00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:33.553
former Trump Secretary of State
Mike Pompeo tried to claim

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:35.187
this would not have happened

00:02:35.187 --> 00:02:36.822
under the previous
administration,

00:02:36.822 --> 00:02:39.525
but got called out
by Fox host Chris Wallace.

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:41.193
-It looks like
the Biden administration

00:02:41.193 --> 00:02:44.731
has just failed in its execution
of its own plan.

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:46.698
The plan should have been
much like we had,

00:02:46.698 --> 00:02:49.234
was that we would have an
orderly, conditions-based way

00:02:49.234 --> 00:02:51.671
to think about how to draw down
our forces there.

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:54.573
I can assure you, were I still
the Secretary of State,

00:02:54.573 --> 00:02:56.342
with a commander-in-chief
like President Trump,

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:58.010
the Taliban
would have understood

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:00.279
that there were
real costs to pay.

00:03:00.279 --> 00:03:03.416
-You were the first American
Secretary of State

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:05.551
to ever meet with the Taliban,

00:03:05.551 --> 00:03:09.655
and you talked about how
they had agreed to join us

00:03:09.655 --> 00:03:11.557
in the fight against terrorism.

00:03:11.557 --> 00:03:15.461
Do you regret giving the Taliban
that legitimacy?

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:18.698
Do you regret
pressing the Afghan government

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:21.300
to release 5,000 prisoners,
which they did,

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:24.169
some of whom are now
back on the battlefield,

00:03:24.169 --> 00:03:27.106
fighting with the Taliban?

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:29.342
-Chris, you make peace
with your enemies.

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:31.744
Chris, we never
trusted the Taliban.

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:33.679
You can ask them yourselves.

00:03:33.679 --> 00:03:36.148
We didn't take the word
of the Taliban.

00:03:36.148 --> 00:03:38.351
We watched their actions
on the ground.

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:39.852
When they did the right thing

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:42.121
and they helped us
against terror,

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:43.322
that was all good.

00:03:43.322 --> 00:03:45.592
And when they didn't,
we crushed them.

00:03:45.592 --> 00:03:47.760
-Alright, first of all, there's
literally a picture of you

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.329
meeting with a Taliban leader

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:51.431
the Trump administration
had released from prison.

00:03:51.431 --> 00:03:54.300
That's from November --
nine months ago.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.969
It's not some ancient photograph
from 30 years ago

00:03:56.969 --> 00:03:58.470
that we had to unearth
by digging through

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:00.205
microfiche
at the National Archives

00:04:00.205 --> 00:04:01.607
and then smuggling it out

00:04:01.607 --> 00:04:03.309
in a rolled-up copy
of the Constitution

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:05.043
like Nick Cage
in "National Treasure,"

00:04:05.043 --> 00:04:06.845
although I would give anything
to hear Nick Cage say

00:04:06.845 --> 00:04:08.047
the word "microfiche."

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:09.148
[As Cage]
There's a secret message,

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:10.749
written by
Benjamin Franklin's ghost,

00:04:10.749 --> 00:04:14.153
and it exists only
on microfiche!"

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:15.588
[ Normal voice ]
"National Treasure" --

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:18.524
three years after the beginning
of the war in Afghanistan.

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:22.094
Second, you think the Trump plan
would have been more orderly

00:04:22.094 --> 00:04:23.428
than what's happening now?

00:04:23.428 --> 00:04:25.798
You guys are the ones
who wanted to withdraw by May.

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:28.300
I have a hard time believing
Trump would have done it

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:29.468
in a more orderly way,

00:04:29.468 --> 00:04:31.470
since nothing he ever did
was orderly.

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:34.973
He couldn't even withdraw from
an umbrella in orderly fashion.

00:04:34.973 --> 00:04:37.310
Instead of armchair generals
engaging in

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:39.612
craven political-point-scoring,
what we need right now is

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:42.148
everyone calling
for the U.S. to accept

00:04:42.148 --> 00:04:44.283
as many Afghan refugees
as possible.

00:04:44.283 --> 00:04:46.419
That includes Afghans
who worked with the U.S. Army,

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:47.854
but it shouldn't be
limited to them.

00:04:47.854 --> 00:04:50.255
We should welcome
anyone who wants to come.

00:04:50.255 --> 00:04:51.990
-What should the Biden
administration be doing

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:54.527
for the people of Afghanistan
right now?

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:59.165
-Every Afghan who
is interested in doing so

00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:02.134
should be given asylum
inside the United States.

00:05:02.134 --> 00:05:03.735
There should be
an urgent process.

00:05:03.735 --> 00:05:07.072
They should be fast-tracked,
and the logistics of it

00:05:07.072 --> 00:05:09.675
can be, in part,
the responsibility

00:05:09.675 --> 00:05:11.777
of one of the greatest
logistical organizations

00:05:11.777 --> 00:05:14.146
on the planet, which is
the United States military,

00:05:14.146 --> 00:05:16.615
and in particular,
the United States Air Force.

00:05:16.615 --> 00:05:19.952
The idea that what the Biden
administration is doing

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:22.388
is helping get out Afghans

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:24.624
who worked for
the United States military

00:05:24.624 --> 00:05:26.759
or served
the United States occupation.

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:30.896
That is a moral floor that is
functioning as a moral ceiling.

00:05:30.896 --> 00:05:33.632
Working with the United States
should not be

00:05:33.632 --> 00:05:35.868
a condition of acceptance

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:38.570
by American
refugee-admissions people.

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:39.771
-That's exactly right.

00:05:39.771 --> 00:05:41.740
Taking in as many
Afghan refugees

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:43.909
as want to come here
and granting them asylum

00:05:43.909 --> 00:05:45.344
is the bare minimum we can do.

00:05:45.344 --> 00:05:47.212
We should be doing it
as fast as possible.

00:05:47.212 --> 00:05:50.315
And we have the logistical
capability to do it.

00:05:50.315 --> 00:05:51.851
I know it's not the same,

00:05:51.851 --> 00:05:53.919
but when I got my vaccine
at a FEMA site,

00:05:53.919 --> 00:05:55.621
I was in and out in 20 minutes

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:57.523
with a shot in my arm
and a CDC card

00:05:57.523 --> 00:05:59.625
that for some reason
doesn't fit in my wallet.

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:01.326
And I know today probably
isn't the right time

00:06:01.326 --> 00:06:02.995
to plug a product, but
I'm excited to announce

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:06.498
MyWallet, the new
awkwardly sized wallet,

00:06:06.498 --> 00:06:09.535
built specifically to
hold your vaccine card.

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:13.972
MyWallet -- order now to receive
a free pair of MyWeirdPants,

00:06:13.972 --> 00:06:18.544
the only pants with pockets
big enough to hold MyWallet.

00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:20.846
Anyway, the point is,
we should be marshaling

00:06:20.846 --> 00:06:24.016
the same logistical prowess to
take in as many Afghan refugees

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:25.818
as possible,
as quickly as possible.

00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:28.287
The priority should be
getting them out now

00:06:28.287 --> 00:06:29.921
and worrying about
the paperwork later.

00:06:29.921 --> 00:06:32.357
And yet, for some reason,
the process for many Afghans,

00:06:32.357 --> 00:06:35.328
including those who worked with
the U.S. has been a nightmare.

00:06:35.328 --> 00:06:37.229
For example,
"The Atlantic" detailed

00:06:37.229 --> 00:06:38.965
the flight of one "interpreter
who worked

00:06:38.965 --> 00:06:40.700
alongside NATO combat units.

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:43.202
His first visa application,
like those of so many others,

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:45.438
was denied on spurious
bureaucratic grounds.

00:06:45.438 --> 00:06:47.606
His second attempt
hung in limbo for years

00:06:47.606 --> 00:06:50.209
as he tried to track down the
human-resources department

00:06:50.209 --> 00:06:52.745
of the military contractor
that had employed him

00:06:52.745 --> 00:06:54.646
and that subsequently
went through

00:06:54.646 --> 00:06:56.782
several changes
of ownership and name."

00:06:56.782 --> 00:06:58.584
Holy [Bleep],
just let him come here.

00:06:58.584 --> 00:07:00.252
Screw the paperwork
and the red tape.

00:07:00.252 --> 00:07:01.587
Why are we putting them through
a process

00:07:01.587 --> 00:07:03.656
that's more complicated
than trying to switch

00:07:03.656 --> 00:07:05.324
your Verizon bill
to a new address.

00:07:05.324 --> 00:07:08.193
"No, I don't want to upgrade
to the Triple Play package.

00:07:08.193 --> 00:07:09.561
I just want to move my service.

00:07:09.561 --> 00:07:11.364
No, I do not want to add
a phone line.

00:07:11.364 --> 00:07:12.498
I'm just moving.

00:07:12.498 --> 00:07:14.233
I do not know
my account PIN number.

00:07:14.233 --> 00:07:16.602
No, I do not know
my 11-digit billing code.

00:07:16.602 --> 00:07:18.404
What's my dog's middle name?

00:07:18.404 --> 00:07:20.973
Hey, what's your middle name?

00:07:20.973 --> 00:07:23.075
He doesn't know."

00:07:23.075 --> 00:07:24.843
And those attempting
to flee now,

00:07:24.843 --> 00:07:26.279
in the face
of the Taliban onslaught,

00:07:26.279 --> 00:07:28.847
are dealing with
the same chaos and confusion,

00:07:28.847 --> 00:07:30.783
as NBC reported
over the weekend.

00:07:30.783 --> 00:07:32.652
-We went to a processing center
today,

00:07:32.652 --> 00:07:36.321
a private kind of pop-up office,

00:07:36.321 --> 00:07:38.890
where there was two people

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:40.859
with a computer
in front of them.

00:07:40.859 --> 00:07:44.096
And the office was packed
with Afghans coming in

00:07:44.096 --> 00:07:46.798
who were trying to navigate
their way

00:07:46.798 --> 00:07:49.868
through the U.S.
State Department's website.

00:07:49.868 --> 00:07:51.370
All the documentation
that they need to provide

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:52.605
is in English.

00:07:52.605 --> 00:07:54.340
They need to be
in multiple copies.

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:55.841
And a lot of the people
who were coming in

00:07:55.841 --> 00:07:57.609
certainly didn't speak English.

00:07:57.609 --> 00:07:58.977
'Cause it's
not just translators.

00:07:58.977 --> 00:08:00.813
You have security guards
and you have contractors

00:08:00.813 --> 00:08:04.049
and cleaners.
Not all of them speak English

00:08:04.049 --> 00:08:06.285
and can navigate their way
through a website.

00:08:06.285 --> 00:08:08.587
-Why are we making this
so [Bleep] complicated?

00:08:08.587 --> 00:08:11.156
You need to navigate
a government website

00:08:11.156 --> 00:08:13.192
with multiple copies
of your personal records

00:08:13.192 --> 00:08:15.594
in a packed office with just
two people at a computer?

00:08:15.594 --> 00:08:19.365
So, basic, it's the DMV.
We just re-created the DMV.

00:08:19.365 --> 00:08:21.767
And no one should ever
have to go through that.

00:08:21.767 --> 00:08:23.135
The last time I was at the DMV,

00:08:23.135 --> 00:08:25.003
I waited in line so long,
I grew a mustache,

00:08:25.003 --> 00:08:27.340
and they ended up putting
the wrong name on my license.

00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:29.508
[ Laughter ]

00:08:29.508 --> 00:08:31.710
And then my license
was too small

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:34.112
to fit in my new MyWallet.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:34.112 --> 00:08:36.415
The tragedy that's unfolding now
is the culmination

00:08:36.415 --> 00:08:38.351
of a two-decade-long legacy
of failure

00:08:38.351 --> 00:08:40.853
left behind by politicians
of both parties

00:08:40.853 --> 00:08:43.222
who repeatedly withheld the
truth from the American people.

00:08:43.222 --> 00:08:45.424
When Bush first announced
the invasion of Afghanistan,

00:08:45.424 --> 00:08:46.925
20 years ago,
the goal at the time,

00:08:46.925 --> 00:08:48.226
according to Bush and

00:08:48.226 --> 00:08:50.028
the politicians
that supported the war,

00:08:50.028 --> 00:08:51.630
was to retaliate
against Al-Qaeda

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:53.699
and the Taliban regime
that was shielding it

00:08:53.699 --> 00:08:55.133
and to prevent future attacks.

00:08:55.133 --> 00:08:56.268
And as the war dragged on,

00:08:56.268 --> 00:08:58.003
Bush continued to insist

00:08:58.003 --> 00:09:00.238
the U.S. was succeeding
in its mission.

00:09:00.238 --> 00:09:02.374
-I said a long time ago,
one of our objectives is

00:09:02.374 --> 00:09:03.609
to smoke 'em out
and get them running

00:09:03.609 --> 00:09:05.244
and bring them to justice.

00:09:05.244 --> 00:09:08.047
We're smoking them out.
They're running.

00:09:08.047 --> 00:09:10.316
And now we're going to
bring them to justice.

00:09:10.316 --> 00:09:12.284
-Remember when the President
routinely used

00:09:12.284 --> 00:09:13.686
the phrase "smoke 'em out"

00:09:13.686 --> 00:09:15.854
like he was in an episode
of "Branded"?

00:09:15.854 --> 00:09:18.490
And I'm sorry to drop
a "Branded" reference,

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:20.292
but sometimes you got to
pander to the people

00:09:20.292 --> 00:09:22.428
who are too old
for the "MASH" jokes.

00:09:22.428 --> 00:09:23.996
[ Laughter ]

00:09:23.996 --> 00:09:26.365
Hope you guys liked it!

00:09:26.365 --> 00:09:28.166
[ Laughter ]
Hmm.

00:09:28.166 --> 00:09:30.035
Throughout the war,
Bush promised

00:09:30.035 --> 00:09:32.838
that the U.S. would not repeat
the history of failure

00:09:32.838 --> 00:09:35.374
that had beset
past empires in Afghanistan.

00:09:35.374 --> 00:09:38.443
-The history of military
conflict in Afghanistan,

00:09:38.443 --> 00:09:43.849
it's been one of initial success
followed by

00:09:43.849 --> 00:09:48.621
long years of floundering
and ultimate failure.

00:09:48.621 --> 00:09:51.724
We're not gonna
repeat that mistake.

00:09:51.724 --> 00:09:53.559
-The very thing they told us
wouldn't happen

00:09:53.559 --> 00:09:55.227
is exactly what happened.
He sounds like

00:09:55.227 --> 00:09:57.296
he's describing his own battle
with a poncho.

00:09:57.296 --> 00:09:58.530
We had some initial success

00:09:58.530 --> 00:10:00.198
followed by floundering
and ultimate failure.

00:10:00.198 --> 00:10:01.667
But we won't be deterred.

00:10:01.667 --> 00:10:03.903
Next, we're gonna try
an umbrella hat.

00:10:03.903 --> 00:10:06.505
[ As Trump ] Umbrellas
aren't easy either.

00:10:06.505 --> 00:10:08.708
Just FYI.
[ Laughter ]

00:10:08.708 --> 00:10:10.409
[ Normal voice ] They knew,
early in the war,

00:10:10.409 --> 00:10:12.144
that the danger of
failure and instability

00:10:12.144 --> 00:10:13.645
was very real,
and behind the scenes,

00:10:13.645 --> 00:10:16.315
they even admitted they had
no idea what to do about it.

00:10:16.315 --> 00:10:18.250
Secretary of Defense
Donald Rumsfeld

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:19.918
wrote in an internal memo,

00:10:19.918 --> 00:10:21.354
only six months
after the war started,

00:10:21.354 --> 00:10:24.423
"We are never going to get the
U.S. military out of Afghanistan

00:10:24.423 --> 00:10:27.292
unless we take care to see
that there is something going on

00:10:27.292 --> 00:10:29.061
that will provide the stability

00:10:29.061 --> 00:10:31.530
that will be necessary
for us to leave."

00:10:31.530 --> 00:10:33.098
"'Help!' he wrote."

00:10:33.098 --> 00:10:34.767
He literally wrote
the word "help"

00:10:34.767 --> 00:10:36.568
with an exclamation point.
You know, the same way

00:10:36.568 --> 00:10:39.038
you text your spouse when you're
trapped in a conversation

00:10:39.038 --> 00:10:41.207
at a dinner party that you
desperately want to get out of.

00:10:41.207 --> 00:10:42.874
"Rick has been talking about
his metal cover band

00:10:42.874 --> 00:10:44.042
for 20 minutes.

00:10:44.042 --> 00:10:46.112
They're called
Age Against the Machine.

00:10:46.112 --> 00:10:47.446
Help!"

00:10:47.446 --> 00:10:48.813
The Bush administration
kicked off

00:10:48.813 --> 00:10:50.983
a 20-year bipartisan tradition
of lying about the war

00:10:50.983 --> 00:10:52.918
in Afghanistan and
shielding the American people

00:10:52.918 --> 00:10:54.620
from the truth
of what was really happening.

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:57.589
We know that from
blockbuster reporting in 2019

00:10:57.589 --> 00:10:59.859
from "The Washington Post,"
which got its hand

00:10:59.859 --> 00:11:01.627
on a confidential trove
of documents

00:11:01.627 --> 00:11:03.028
called "The Afghanistan Papers,"

00:11:03.028 --> 00:11:05.964
in which senior U.S. officials
from both parties

00:11:05.964 --> 00:11:08.133
admitted they'd been lying
about the reality

00:11:08.133 --> 00:11:09.968
about how the war
was really going.

00:11:09.968 --> 00:11:11.637
For example,
a three-star Army general

00:11:11.637 --> 00:11:14.073
who served as the White House's
Afghan war czar

00:11:14.073 --> 00:11:16.341
during the Bush and Obama
administration,

00:11:16.341 --> 00:11:19.178
said in 2015, "We were devoid

00:11:19.178 --> 00:11:22.147
of a fundamental understanding
of Afghanistan --

00:11:22.147 --> 00:11:23.916
we didn't know
what we were doing.

00:11:23.916 --> 00:11:25.651
What are we trying to do here?

00:11:25.651 --> 00:11:27.653
We didn't have
the foggiest notion

00:11:27.653 --> 00:11:29.221
of what we were undertaking."

00:11:29.221 --> 00:11:31.690
The U.S.
foreign-policy apparatus

00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:34.593
should not approach Afghanistan
the same way I approached

00:11:34.593 --> 00:11:36.729
trying to install
a wireless router.

00:11:36.729 --> 00:11:39.030
"Connect the router
to a broadband gateway

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:41.567
from your ISP
by inserting the Ethernet cable

00:11:41.567 --> 00:11:44.036
to the port located
on the back of the TP-Link?

00:11:44.036 --> 00:11:46.705
I don't have the foggiest notion
of what I'm undertaking!

00:11:46.705 --> 00:11:49.074
Do you know how this works?
Why am I asking you?"

00:11:49.074 --> 00:11:51.010
And instead of being honest

00:11:51.010 --> 00:11:52.811
and telling that
to the American people,

00:11:52.811 --> 00:11:54.980
officials cherry-picked and
misrepresented the data

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:56.615
to make the war look
like it was going

00:11:56.615 --> 00:11:57.950
much better
than it actually was.

00:11:57.950 --> 00:12:00.219
For example, an Army colonel
who served

00:12:00.219 --> 00:12:02.221
as a senior
counter-insurgency adviser

00:12:02.221 --> 00:12:05.457
to U.S. military commanders
in 2013 and '14

00:12:05.457 --> 00:12:09.328
told government interviewers,
"Every data point was altered

00:12:09.328 --> 00:12:11.263
to present
the best picture possible."

00:12:11.263 --> 00:12:13.532
"Surveys, for instance,
were totally unreliable

00:12:13.532 --> 00:12:16.301
but reinforced that everything
we were doing was right

00:12:16.301 --> 00:12:19.004
and we became a self-licking
ice cream cone."

00:12:19.004 --> 00:12:23.175
What? Is that a thing?
A self-licking ice cream cone?

00:12:23.175 --> 00:12:24.843
That sounds like something
that would get pitched

00:12:24.843 --> 00:12:27.346
on an episode of "Shark Tank"
where everyone laughs

00:12:27.346 --> 00:12:29.681
but then Mark Cuban invests,
and three years later,

00:12:29.681 --> 00:12:32.484
you hear that it somehow
sold for $1 billion to Apple,

00:12:32.484 --> 00:12:33.886
and go to a party,
and all your friends

00:12:33.886 --> 00:12:35.654
have self-licking
ice cream cones.

00:12:35.654 --> 00:12:37.756
"Try it. It's called the iCone.
It's Siri-enabled.

00:12:37.756 --> 00:12:39.424
It tracks your steps."

00:12:39.424 --> 00:12:41.126
The majority of Americans

00:12:41.126 --> 00:12:43.429
want the forever war
in Afghanistan to end.

00:12:43.429 --> 00:12:45.063
Should have ended
a long time ago.

00:12:45.063 --> 00:12:46.732
Ending it now
is the only option.

00:12:46.732 --> 00:12:49.701
The one thing we can and must do
right now

00:12:49.701 --> 00:12:53.305
is accept as many refugees
and grant as many Afghans asylum

00:12:53.305 --> 00:12:56.208
as we possibly can,
as quickly as we can.

00:12:56.208 --> 00:12:58.544
And if there's anyone left
in politics and the media

00:12:58.544 --> 00:13:00.412
who disagrees, who fearmongers

00:13:00.412 --> 00:13:02.380
about taking in
as many refugees as we can,

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:04.616
then when election time comes,
I hope voters will...

00:13:04.616 --> 00:13:05.650
-Smoke 'em out.

00:13:05.650 --> 00:13:07.652
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:13:07.652 --> 00:13:11.056
[ Theme music plays ]

00:13:11.056 --> 00:13:12.757
God's Love We Deliver
cooks and brings

00:13:12.757 --> 00:13:15.561
over 2 million meals a year
to men, women, and children

00:13:15.561 --> 00:13:18.163
living with HIV/AIDS, cancer,
and other serious illnesses,

00:13:18.163 --> 00:13:19.798
and they need your help
now more than ever.

00:13:19.798 --> 00:13:22.167
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the Donate button.

00:13:22.167 --> 00:13:24.570
Stay safe, get vaccinated.
We love you.

